    """ For a given list of input numbers, calculate Mean Absolute Deviation
    squared around the mean of this dataset.
    Mean Absolute Deviation is the average of squares of the differences
    between each element and centerpoint (mean in this case):
    SMADE = Average (( x - x_mean ) ** 2 )
    >>> square_mean_absolute_deviation([1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0])
    1.25
